{
  "body_human_readable": "### Tesla's 2024 Vehicle Deliveries Mark First Annual Decline in Over a Decade\n\nTesla announced its full-year vehicle delivery numbers for 2024, revealing a total of 1,789,226 vehicles delivered worldwide. This figure marks the first time in over a decade that the electric vehicle giant has seen a year-over-year decline in deliveries, down 1.07% from 1,808,581 vehicles in 2023.\n\nDespite the annual dip, Tesla reported a record-breaking fourth quarter, with 495,570 vehicles delivered. This was an all-time high for quarterly deliveries.\n\nBreaking down the numbers for the full year, deliveries of the Model 3 and Model Y accounted for the vast majority of sales, totaling 1,704,093 vehicles. The \"other models\" category, which includes the Model S, Model X, and the newly launched Cybertruck, saw 85,133 deliveries. Total production for the year reached 1,773,443 vehicles.\n\nThe slight decline in annual deliveries has been attributed to a variety of factors, including an arson attack at its Berlin factory, shipping diversions, and a general slowdown in the growth of the electric vehicle market.\n\nIn the fourth quarter of 2024, Tesla also reached a historic milestone, delivering its 7 millionth vehicle since its inception. Looking ahead, the company has indicated plans to update all its factories for the new Model Y, which is expected to cause several weeks of lost production in the first quarter of 2025.",
